WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:12.060
Seventy-nine. Headphones and Hearing. The music you love could end up making you deaf.

2
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:18.860
More specifically, the way you listen to the music you love could be making you deaf faster.

3
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:26.660
The problem is headphones. In the past, we played music out into the air. Then, earmuff-style

4
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:33.140
headphones were invented, and we were able to play music much closer to our ears. Now

5
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:40.100
we have earbuds, and people are starting to get worried. Many doctors think earbuds are

6
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:47.860
worse than older headphones because they play music directly into the ears. Also, earbuds

7
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:53.300
are not as good at blocking outside noise, so people who use them may turn the volume

8
00:00:53.300 --> 00:01:00.420
up to dangerous levels. What's a dangerous noise level? Well, it depends on how long you're going

9
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:07.700
to listen to the noise. This is the next problem. Very, very loud sounds can be dangerous to your

10
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:14.340
hearing, even if you only listen to them for a few minutes. But the scary truth is that even

11
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:21.380
normal-seeming noise can be dangerous if you listen to it all the time. People, especially

12
00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:27.700
young people, wear headphones all day long nowadays. Even if your music isn't blasting,

13
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:34.020
listening to it for many hours this way can damage your hearing. Noise-induced hearing loss,

14
00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:39.940
the kind that headphones cause, happens when tiny hairs in your ear canal become overstressed and

15
00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:47.940
die. Guess what? Playing loud music only millimeters away from these tiny hairs can stress them out,

16
00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:54.340
and once these hairs die, they may not come back. Hearing loss is usually permanent.

17
00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.860
Think for a minute about how long you spend listening to headphones and other loud noises

18
00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:06.900
every day. Then do some research. There are resources online to tell you what volumes are

19
00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:12.180
safe and for how long. Don't take your hearing for granted.
